[32m+[m[32m# 🚀 Deployment Guide[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe **Gradio KYC app** (`app/gradio_app.py`) is the primary web entry point for[m
[32m+[m[32mdeployment. It reads the `PORT` environment variable and binds to `0.0.0.0`, so[m
[32m+[m[32mit works out-of-the-box on every platform below. Provide your trained checkpoint[m
[32m+[m[32mat `models/best_xception_celebdf.pth` (gitignored) or set `DEEPFAKE_CHECKPOINT`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEntry points:[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Gradio UI** → `python app/gradio_app.py` (port 7860 locally, `$PORT` in cloud)[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Streamlit UI** → `streamlit run app/streamlit_app.py` (8501)[m
[32m+[m[32m- **REST API** → `uvicorn api.main:app` (8000, Swagger at `/docs`)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1) 🤗 Hugging Face Spaces (Gradio SDK)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSpaces reads front matter from the repo's `README.md`. Because our default[m
[32m+[m[32m`app.py` is the Streamlit app, point the Space at the Gradio file with[m
[32m+[m[32m`app_file`. Create the Space (SDK = Gradio) and make its `README.md` start with:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```yaml[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m[32mtitle: Deepfake Detection KYC[m
[32m+[m[32memoji: 🕵️[m
[32m+[m[32mcolorFrom: indigo[m
[32m+[m[32mcolorTo: purple[m
[32m+[m[32msdk: gradio[m
[32m+[m[32msdk_version: 6.20.0[m
[32m+[m[32mapp_file: app/gradio_app.py[m
[32m+[m[32mpinned: false[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSteps:[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Create a new **Gradio** Space on huggingface.co.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Push this repository to it (`git remote add space https://huggingface.co/spaces/<user>/<name>` → `git push space main`).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Upload the checkpoint to the Space (via the UI or `huggingface_hub`), or load[m
[32m+[m[32m   it from the Hub at startup.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. The Space installs `requirements.txt` and launches `app/gradio_app.py`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> Tip: for GPU, select a GPU hardware tier in the Space settings; the app uses[m
[32m+[m[32m> CUDA automatically when available.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2) 🎨 Render[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA blueprint is provided in **`render.yaml`**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Push the repo to GitHub.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Render dashboard → **New + → Blueprint** → select this repo.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Render builds (installs CPU PyTorch + `requirements.txt`) and runs[m
[32m+[m[32m   `python app/gradio_app.py`, injecting `$PORT`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNotes:[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use at least the **Starter** plan — PyTorch needs more memory/build time than[m
[32m+[m[32m  the free tier allows.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add the checkpoint via a **persistent disk** mounted at `models/`, or bake it[m
[32m+[m[32m  into a custom Docker image (Render also supports `Dockerfile` deploys).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3) 🚄 Railway[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mConfig is provided in **`railway.json`** (Nixpacks) and **`Procfile`**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. `railway init` (or connect the GitHub repo in the Railway dashboard).[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Railway builds with Nixpacks and runs `python app/gradio_app.py`.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. It injects `$PORT`, which the app honours.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo run the **API** instead of the UI, change the start command to[m
[32m+[m[32m`uvicorn api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT` (see the `api` line in `Procfile`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4) 🐳 Docker / Docker Compose[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSingle container (Gradio):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mdocker build -t deepfake-detection .[m
[32m+[m[32mdocker run -p 7860:7860 -e PORT=7860 \[m
[32m+[m[32m    -v $(pwd)/models:/app/models \[m
[32m+[m[32m    deepfake-detection python app/gradio_app.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll services at once (API + Streamlit + Gradio):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mdocker compose up --build[m
[32m+[m[32m# API     -> http://localhost:8000/docs[m
[32m+[m[32m# Streamlit -> http://localhost:8501[m
[32m+[m[32m# Gradio  -> http://localhost:7860[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`.dockerignore` keeps datasets and runtime artifacts out of the build context.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Environment variables[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Variable | Default | Purpose |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `PORT` | `7860` | Web port (set automatically by Render/Railway/HF) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_CHECKPOINT` | `models/best_xception_celebdf.pth` | Model weights path |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_CHECKPOINT_URL` | _(unset)_ | Direct HTTPS URL to auto-download weights on startup |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_HF_REPO` | _(unset)_ | Hugging Face repo id to auto-download weights from |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_HF_FILENAME` | checkpoint basename | File to fetch from the HF repo |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_HF_REVISION` | _(unset)_ | Optional HF branch/tag/commit |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_MODEL_NAME` | `xception` | Backbone architecture |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_FACE_DETECTOR` | `mtcnn` | `mtcnn`, `haar`, or `auto` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_DB` | `results/predictions.db` | SQLite history location |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_API_KEY` | _(unset)_ | If set, inference endpoints require header `X-API-Key` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_RATE_LIMIT` | `0` | Max requests/min per client (0 = unlimited) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_ADMIN_USER` | `admin` | Default UI login username (bootstrapped on first run) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_ADMIN_PASSWORD` | `admin123` | Default UI login password — **change in production** |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `DEEPFAKE_DISABLE_LOGIN` | _(unset)_ | Set to `1` to disable the Gradio login page (public demo) |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Checkpoint auto-download (recommended for cloud)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`models/*.pth` is gitignored (weights are large). Instead of baking the file in,[m
[32m+[m[32mlet the app fetch it on first startup by setting **one** of these env vars:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m# Option A — direct URL (no extra dependency)[m
[32m+[m[32mexport DEEPFAKE_CHECKPOINT_URL="https://example.com/best_xception_celebdf.pth"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Option B — Hugging Face Hub (needs huggingface_hub, already in requirements.txt)[m
[32m+[m[32mexport DEEPFAKE_HF_REPO="your-username/deepfake-xception"[m
[32m+[m[32m# export DEEPFAKE_HF_FILENAME="best_xception_celebdf.pth"   # defaults to the checkpoint basename[m
[32m+[m[32m# export DEEPFAKE_HF_REVISION="main"                        # optional[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe first prediction (or `python -m src.checkpoint`) downloads the file to[m
[32m+[m[32m`models/` and every entry point — Gradio, Streamlit, FastAPI, CLI — uses it.[m
[32m+[m[32mTrigger it manually with:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m src.checkpoint[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWithout a checkpoint (and no download source), the apps still start and render[m
[32m+[m[32mbut show a clear "model not found" message instead of predictions.[m
